    {
      "id": "42370fd9-1edd-81d0-a48d-e66d6c81f924",
      "title": "Nano Nagle Place · Culture Night Cork",
      "slug": "ceangailte-nano-nagle-2026",
      "description": "Ceangailte at Nano Nagle Place for Culture Night in Cork, shown at the same time as at Unframe Festival in Berlin, with a live connection between the two venues.",
      "bodyHtml": "<p>Ceangailte explores how media representations shape narratives of colonialism, oppression, and resilience through a dynamic dual-screen display, immersive audio, and sculptural elements. Drawing on the Irish word ceangailte (“tied”, “connected”, or “bound”), the installation brings together perspectives from former colonies of Empire, reflecting on power structures, resistance, and aspirations for freedom. By juxtaposing mainstream narratives with lived realities, the work invites audiences to consider the gap between what is publicly presented and what is pursued behind the scenes.</p><p>Ceangailte was shown at the same time in Cork and Berlin: here at Nano Nagle Place for Culture Night, and at Unframe Festival in Berlin. A live connection between the two venues was a small, symbolic gesture towards the connections the work is about.</p><p>Showing it in both cities connects where the two of us came from with where the idea for Ceangailte was first conceived. Both Culture Night in Cork and Unframe Festival in Berlin share values of solidarity and a desire for change, which the work reflects.</p>",
      "properties": {
        "venueAddress": "Global Hub, Nano Nagle Place, Douglas Street, Cork",
        "country": "Ireland",
        "date": "2026-09-18",
        "dateEnd": "2026-09-20",
